WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:02.120
Overlord has arrived.

00:00:02.129 --> 00:00:07.100
Director Julius Avery's mash-up of drama at
the turning point of World War II and Nazi

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:12.780
science experiments straight out of Wolfenstein
is finally here, riding a strong wave of critical

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:17.280
buzz as it lands in theaters for viewers eager
for a little pulpy period horror.

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:19.760
How deep do those Nazi experiments go?

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:22.760
Let's find out as we dissect the ending of
Overlord.

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:25.840
Spoilers ahead, obviously it's a minefield
out there.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:30.520
Before our reluctant heroes from the U.S.
Army even get a whiff of what's going on in

00:00:30.529 --> 00:00:34.829
the lab beneath the village's church, they
enter the home of Chloe, who lives with what

00:00:34.829 --> 00:00:37.390
she describes as a "very sick" aunt.

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:41.579
We figure out what's up pretty quickly, and
Chloe confirms that the illness is actually

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:45.240
the result of experimentation done by the
Nazis at the church.

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:48.980
Then the action picks up, and the aunt's illness
is barely mentioned again.

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:53.440
While our heroes are busy blowing up the lab,
though, it's hard not to wonder: How many

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:57.880
people did the Nazis experiment on only to
release back to their homes at some point?

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:01.600
How many of them are there, and how far back
does that trail stretch?

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:05.940
Even if the lab itself is gone, the victims
aren't, and its seems likely that someone

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:07.860
from the Allied Forces will find them.

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:13.060
As Boyce and his compatriots dig further into
what's really going on beneath the church,

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:18.170
they discover that the mysterious experiments
are all based on a substance that occurs underground

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:22.930
naturally, somehow having the capability to
reanimate dead bodies and supercharge live

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:24.600
ones if properly refined.

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:27.520
"What is this?"

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:33.030
The Nazis haven't perfected the process yet,
but the serum clearly has some powerful effects,

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:34.760
and they seem to have a constant supply.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:39.640
By the end of the film, the lab is gone, but
if the zombie-making tar was there all along,

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:42.420
isn't it possible that there's a good deal
more of it down there?

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:44.940
What's so special about this particular place?

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:49.200
If this much progress has been made in this
one French village, it's likely that other

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:53.170
Nazis are aware of the tar's capabilities,
and they're already looking for more elsewhere

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:55.670
in Europe and there may well be more out there.

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:59.570
The lab might be destroyed, but the search
for the substance that can grant a Thousand

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:01.400
Year Reich is definitely not.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:06.060
It's clear from what little we know of the
Nazis' actual scientific process that there's

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:10.280
been a lot of trial and error involved in
the serum they're developing, and we don't

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:14.260
actually know how they realized they could
use the tar beneath the church for that purpose

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:15.260
in the first place.

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:20.200
Overlord is a film that plays on reports of
secret Nazi programs geared towards all sorts

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:23.080
of occult things, so the film can get away
with a lot.

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:27.400
This atmosphere — plus the strange dead
animal the soldiers discover in the woods

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:31.590
— hint that there were definitely experiments
of a different kind in this village before

00:02:31.590 --> 00:02:32.940
the serum was developed.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:35.960
Was the doctor up to some kind of gene splicing?

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:38.600
Was he trying to create hybrid war dogs of
some kind?

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:43.260
We don't know, but the Nazis' sloppy operation
implies that there's more to be found out

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:45.000
there than just human zombies.

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:50.280
Overlord takes as many genre liberties as
it wants, but it also follows certain war

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:55.100
movie structural conventions — and perhaps
nowhere is that more evident than in the story

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:59.100
of Chloe and her little brother Paul, who
bond with the soldiers after they hole up

00:02:59.100 --> 00:02:59.880
in their house.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:03.340
A romantic connection between Boyce and Chloe
is heavily implied.

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:04.340
What happens now?

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:07.580
Do the soldiers just move on and leave these
two to rebuild their lives?

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:12.500
They might be separated temporarily, but the
bonding experience of the mission and Boyce's

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:16.460
sensitive soul makes them being apart permanently
seem unlikely.

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:20.320
He might march on to Berlin, sure, but we
feel like he'll be back eventually to get

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:22.060
to know the French girl a little better.

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:26.640
At the beginning of Overlord, Ford is the
rough, cynical officer who's been through

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:31.430
hell and isn't about to go soft for anyone,
while Boyce is the innocent young trainee

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:35.940
who's terrified of war and once proved himself
too sensitive to even kill a mouse.

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:40.130
By the end of the film, Ford is dead, and
Boyce has absorbed many of his lessons.

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:44.620
He's capable of killing, thinking on his feet,
and winning in a hard fight, even if much

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:47.120
of his innocence and compassion has been preserved.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:51.240
We get the sense that Boyce isn't likely to
just leave Chloe in the village forever, but

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:53.140
what about the rest of his military career?

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:57.720
If the film adheres to the same World War
II timeline as the real world, then Boyce

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:01.870
still has nearly a year of fighting left to
do, and then he might be left in Europe to

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:04.760
clean up after the Nazis when Germany surrenders.

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:08.300
He's had experience with the supernatural
now, even if he's not telling anyone about

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:08.800
it.

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:13.520
Will he just leave that in his past, or will
he be keeping an eye open for other Nazi facilities

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:16.680
like the one beneath the church, ready to
strike as necessary?

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:18.380
We're betting on the latter.

